// 2분 분량(약 200단어) 모범 답안과 추가 문항. index.html의 UNIV·TOPICS 다음, 앱 코드 앞에서 불러옴.
// - 기존 문항: 원래 모범 답안(약 95단어)은 짧은 답안 s로 옮기고, LONG을 새 모범 답안 m으로 씀.
// - 새 문항(MORE)은 각 주제 끝에 붙임. 문장 진도 id(주제:문항:문장)가 바뀌지 않게 하려는 것.
// - {NAME} 같은 자리는 '내 정보'로 채워짐.

const LONG = {
"intro:0":"Hi, my name is {NAME}, and I’m {AGE} years old. Let me tell you a little bit about myself. I work for {COMPANY} as {A_JOB}, and I’ve been working there for about {YEARS}. My job is pretty busy, and sometimes I have to work late, but I really like my team. My coworkers are friendly, and we help each other a lot. I live in an apartment in {TOWN} with my family. It’s not a big place, but it’s cozy, and it’s close to the subway station, so my commute is pretty easy. In my free time, I like watching movies and going for a walk in the park near my place. Walking really helps me relieve stress, especially after a long day at work. On weekends, I usually catch up on sleep, meet my friends, or try a new restaurant in my neighborhood. These days, I’m also trying to study English, because I’d like to get promoted and work with people from other countries someday. As for my personality, I think I’m a friendly and easygoing person. I get along with people easily, and I don’t get upset over small things. Anyway, that’s a little bit about me. Thank you.",

"home:0":"I live in a three-bedroom apartment on the tenth floor. It’s not very big, but it’s really comfortable, and I’ve lived there for about seven years. When you walk in, there’s a small entrance where we keep our shoes. Then there’s a living room on the right with a big sofa, a TV, and a few plants by the window. The kitchen is right next to the living room, and it has a small table where my family eats breakfast together. There’s a big window in the living room, so it gets a lot of sunlight in the morning. That’s actually my favorite thing about our place. The bedrooms are down a short hallway. My parents use the biggest one, and my room is at the end. My room is small, but it’s cozy and quiet. I have a desk, a bed, a bookshelf, and a little speaker for music. Compared to my old house, this apartment is much newer and brighter. The only problem is that it doesn’t have much storage space, so it gets messy sometimes. But overall, I really like my home. It’s the place where I can relax and be myself. That’s about it.",
"home:1":"On weekdays, I don’t have much time at home because I work until about six thirty. I usually get home around seven. The first thing I do is take a shower, because it helps me switch off from work. Then I have dinner with my family. We usually talk about our day while we eat. After dinner, I wash the dishes, and then I have some free time. Most of the time, I watch YouTube or Netflix to relax. These days, I’m into a crime drama, so I watch one or two episodes a night. Sometimes I read a book or study English for about thirty minutes instead. I go to bed around midnight, although I know I should sleep earlier. On weekends, it’s quite different. I sleep in until about ten, and I have a late breakfast. Then I clean my room and do the laundry, because I don’t have time for chores during the week. In the afternoon, I just lie on the sofa and take it easy, or I order some food and watch a movie. Honestly, weekends at home are my favorite time of the week. They help me recharge for the next week. That’s what I usually do at home.",
"home:2":"I still remember when I changed the wallpaper in my room last year. The old wallpaper was really dark and old-fashioned. It had a brown flower pattern, and it made the room look small and gloomy. I always felt a little depressed when I came home, so I finally decided to change it myself. I didn’t want to pay a lot of money, so I watched some YouTube videos to learn how to do it. Then I went to a store and chose a light gray color. My brother said he would help me, so we started on a Saturday morning. First, we moved all the furniture out of the room. Then we took off the old wallpaper, which was much harder than I expected. After that, we put up the new one. Honestly, we made a lot of mistakes, and some parts were a little crooked. It took about two days to finish, and we were exhausted. But in the end, it turned out great. Now my room looks much brighter and bigger, and I feel happy whenever I walk in. It was tiring, but it was a really rewarding experience, and I’m proud that we did it ourselves.",

"neighborhood:0":"I live in a quiet neighborhood in {TOWN}. I’ve lived here for about five years, and I really like it. First of all, it’s very convenient. It’s only five minutes from the subway station, so it’s easy to get around. There are lots of restaurants, cafés, and a big supermarket near my apartment, so I can get everything I need on foot. There’s also a small park where people walk their dogs or jog in the evening. Most of the people here are families with kids, so it’s pretty peaceful, and you can see children playing outside after school. On weekends, there’s a small farmers’ market near the station, and I sometimes buy fruit there. Compared to when I first moved in, the neighborhood has changed a lot. There used to be a lot of old buildings, but now there are new apartments and nice coffee shops. The only problem is that parking is a little difficult, especially at night. Also, rent has gone up quite a bit. But overall, it’s a really convenient and comfortable place to live. I’m happy here, and I don’t think I’ll move anytime soon. That’s my neighborhood.",
"neighborhood:1":"In my neighborhood, I usually go to three places. First, I often go to the supermarket near my place to buy groceries. I usually go after work on Wednesdays and on Saturday mornings. I walk there because everything is close, and it only takes about five minutes. I usually buy fruit, vegetables, milk, and some snacks. Second, there’s a gym in my building, so I work out there two or three times a week after work. I mostly do cardio, like running on the treadmill, and some light weights. It’s really convenient, because I don’t have to go outside, even when it’s raining. And third, on weekends, I go to a café near the station with my friends. It’s a small café with really good coffee and cakes. We chat for hours about work, family, and our plans. Also, in the evening, I sometimes take a walk around the block to clear my head. Most of the time I go alone and listen to music, but sometimes my mom comes with me, and we talk about our day. I think my neighborhood is a big part of my daily life. That’s where I usually go.",
"neighborhood:2":"I still remember the time when there was a big festival in my neighborhood. It happened about two years ago, in the fall. The weather was perfect, not too hot and not too cold. There were food trucks and live music everywhere, and the streets were full of people. I went there with my family after dinner. First, we walked around and tried some street food, like tteokbokki, grilled corn, and fish cakes. Everything was delicious. Then we watched a band play on a small stage. They were really good, and everyone was singing along. While we were walking around, something unexpected happened. I ran into some old friends from middle school. I hadn’t seen them in almost ten years, so at first I didn’t even recognize them. But one of them called my name, and I was really surprised. We sat down at a table, ordered some drinks, and talked for hours about the old days. We even exchanged numbers and promised to meet again. Since then, we’ve met a few more times. It was one of the best nights I’ve had in a long time, and I still smile when I think about it.",

"movies:0":"I really enjoy going to the movies. I go about twice a month, usually on weekends with my friends or sometimes alone. I like action movies and comedies the most. Action movies are exciting, and comedies are fun, so they both help me forget about stress. After a long week at work, I just want to laugh or watch something exciting, not think too much. My favorite actor is Ma Dong-seok. He’s famous for his strong image, but his movies are funny too. My favorite one is The Roundup. I’ve seen it three times. I also like Marvel movies, because the special effects look amazing on a big screen. On the other hand, I’m not really into horror movies. They’re too scary for me, and I can’t sleep afterward. So when my friends want to watch a horror movie, I usually suggest something else. I also don’t like really slow movies, because I tend to fall asleep. These days, I watch a lot of movies at home on Netflix, too, because it’s cheaper. But I still think watching a movie in a theater is a special experience. The sound and the big screen make a big difference. That’s why I still go to the movies.",
"movies:1":"When I go to the movies, I usually follow the same routine. First, I check the reviews online, because I don’t want to waste my money on a bad movie. Then I book a ticket on the app. I always choose a seat in the middle, a little toward the back, because that’s where the screen looks best. On the day, I get to the theater about fifteen minutes early. I always buy popcorn and a Coke, because honestly, a movie without popcorn feels strange to me. I usually get the sweet caramel popcorn. Then I find my seat and watch the trailers. During the movie, I turn off my phone so I can focus, and I try not to talk. I really hate it when people use their phones in the theater. After the movie, my friends and I usually go to a restaurant nearby and talk about it over dinner. We talk about our favorite scenes, the actors, and whether the ending was good or not. Sometimes we disagree, and it turns into a fun debate. If the movie was really good, I look up more information about it on the way home. That’s my usual routine when I go to the movies.",
"movies:2":"The most memorable movie I’ve seen is Parasite. I watched it in a theater with a close friend in 2019, right after it came out. Before I watched it, I didn’t know much about the story. I just knew it was directed by Bong Joon-ho and that it had won a big award. It’s about two families from very different backgrounds. One family is very rich, and the other is very poor. The poor family slowly gets jobs in the rich family’s house by lying about who they are. At first, I thought it was just a comedy, because the first half was really funny. Everyone in the theater was laughing. But the story was full of surprises. In the second half, it got really dark and intense, and I couldn’t take my eyes off the screen. I was shocked by the ending, and nobody in the theater said a word when it finished. After the movie, my friend and I sat in a café and talked about it for two hours. It made me think about the gap between rich and poor in our society. Later, it won the Oscar for Best Picture, and I felt really proud as a Korean. That’s why it left such a strong impression on me.",

"music:0":"I love listening to music. I listen to it almost every day. I mostly listen to K-pop and pop songs because they’re catchy and upbeat, and they put me in a good mood. My favorite singer is IU. Her voice is really clear and beautiful, and her lyrics are very touching. I’ve been a fan of hers for more than ten years. My favorite song of hers is Through the Night. It’s a calm, quiet song, and it always makes me feel comfortable. I even went to one of her concerts a few years ago, and it was amazing. I also like some American pop singers, like Ed Sheeran and Bruno Mars. Their songs are fun, and I sometimes learn English expressions from the lyrics. Besides that, I like calm music like jazz, especially when I study or work. It helps me focus, because there are no lyrics to distract me. On the other hand, I don’t really listen to heavy metal. It’s too loud for me. For me, music is a big part of my life. It helps me relax after a long day, it makes my commute less boring, and it always lifts my mood. I can’t imagine my life without music. That’s about it.",
"music:1":"I listen to music almost every day, in many different places. Mostly, I listen to music on my way to work. It takes about forty minutes by subway, so music makes the time go faster. I use my smartphone and wireless earbuds. They have noise canceling, so I can’t hear the noise on the subway at all. I usually use a streaming app like Melon. I pay about ten thousand won a month, and I can listen to any song I want. In the morning, I listen to upbeat songs to wake myself up. At work, I sometimes listen to calm music with one earbud when I need to focus. At home, I play music on a Bluetooth speaker while I cook or clean. It makes boring chores much more fun. I also make my own playlists for different moods, like a workout playlist, a rainy-day playlist, and a sleep playlist. Before I go to bed, I listen to some quiet songs for about twenty minutes. Compared to the past, it’s much more convenient now. When I was a student, I had to download MP3 files one by one. Now I can find any song in seconds. That’s how I usually listen to music.",
"music:2":"My taste in music has changed a lot over the years. When I was in middle school, I mostly listened to K-pop idol groups, like Big Bang and Girls’ Generation. Everyone at school liked them, so I did too. Then, when I was in high school, I got into hip-hop. I loved the strong beats and the lyrics, because they felt honest and cool. I even tried rapping with my friends and wrote some lyrics, although they were pretty bad. But after I started working, my taste changed again. These days, I prefer softer music, like ballads, acoustic songs, and jazz. Loud music makes me tired now, especially after a long day at work. When I get home, I just want something calm and relaxing. I think my taste changed as I got older and my life got busier. When I was young, I wanted music that gave me energy. Now I want music that helps me rest. Interestingly, I still listen to some old hip-hop songs from my high school days when I work out. They remind me of good memories. So I guess my taste didn’t completely change. It just grew wider. That’s how my taste in music has changed.",

"park:0":"There’s a big park about ten minutes from my house, and I go there quite often. It has a long walking trail that goes all the way around a small lake in the middle. There are lots of tall trees and benches along the trail, so people can sit and rest in the shade. On one side, there’s a playground for kids and some exercise machines for adults. On the other side, there’s a large field where people have picnics or play badminton. There’s also a small café near the entrance, where you can buy coffee and ice cream. The park looks different in every season. In spring, it’s full of cherry blossoms, and it’s really beautiful. In summer, it’s green and lively, and in fall, the leaves turn red and yellow. In winter, it’s quiet, and sometimes the lake freezes. The park is always crowded on weekends with families, couples, and people walking their dogs. On weekdays, it’s much quieter. I like it because it feels peaceful, even though it’s in the middle of the city. Whenever I’m there, I feel relaxed and refreshed. I think it’s the best place in my neighborhood. That’s the park I often go to.",
"park:1":"I usually go to the park after dinner, about three times a week. Before I leave home, I change into comfortable clothes and running shoes, and I grab my earbuds and a small bottle of water. When I get to the park, I start by stretching for a few minutes near the entrance. Then I walk around the lake two or three times. It takes about forty minutes. While I walk, I listen to podcasts or music. These days, I listen to an English podcast, because it’s a good way to study without feeling stressed. After that, I use the exercise machines for a few minutes to stretch my back and shoulders, because they get stiff from sitting at my desk all day. Sometimes I just sit on a bench and relax and watch people. It’s fun to see kids playing and dogs running around. On weekends, it’s a little different. I sometimes go with my family in the afternoon and bring some snacks, like kimbap and fruit. We sit on a mat in the field and chat for a while. It takes about an hour in total. It’s a simple routine, but it really helps me stay healthy and clear my mind. That’s what I usually do at the park.",
"park:2":"I still remember something unexpected that happened at the park last summer. It was a hot Sunday evening, and I was walking around the lake as usual. Suddenly, I saw a small puppy sitting alone under a bench. It was a little white dog with a red collar. It was shaking and looked really scared. I looked around for the owner, but nobody was there. At first, I didn’t know what to do. I was worried that it might run into the road. So I sat down next to it, talked to it softly, and gave it some water from my bottle. After a few minutes, it calmed down, and I checked its collar. Luckily, there was a phone number on it. I called the number, and a woman answered in a panic. She said she had been looking for her dog for an hour. I told her where I was, and she came running in ten minutes. When she saw her dog, she almost cried. She thanked me so many times, and she even tried to give me some money, but I said no. It was a small thing, but it made me feel really good all day. Since then, I always look around more carefully at the park.",

"travel:0":"Last year, I traveled to Osaka, Japan, with two of my friends. It was my first trip abroad in about three years, so I was really excited. It’s only a ninety-minute flight from Seoul, so it was easy to get there, and the tickets weren’t too expensive. Osaka is a big and lively city. The streets were very clean, and the people were really kind and polite. Even when we got lost, people tried to help us, although we couldn’t speak Japanese. We stayed there for four days. We visited Osaka Castle, which was really impressive, and we spent a whole day at Universal Studios. The Harry Potter area was my favorite. But honestly, the best part was the food. It was amazing, especially the ramen and takoyaki. We ate all day long, from the morning to late at night. We also went to Dotonbori, a famous street full of restaurants and bright signs. At night, it looked really cool. The city is also great for shopping, so I bought some snacks and clothes for my family. Compared to Seoul, it felt a little slower and more relaxed. I had a really good time there, and I’d love to go back someday.",
"travel:1":"Before a trip, I usually prepare step by step, because I don’t like surprises when I travel. First, I decide where to go and book a flight. I try to book at least two months early, because it’s much cheaper. I usually compare prices on a few different apps. Then I look for a hotel near the station, so it’s easy to get around. I always read the reviews carefully, especially about cleanliness. After that, I search for famous places and restaurants on blogs and YouTube, and I make a simple schedule. I don’t plan every minute, though. I like to leave some free time to just walk around. About a week before the trip, I exchange some money and buy travel insurance. I also buy a SIM card or a pocket Wi-Fi so I can use my phone abroad. A few days before, I check the weather and decide what clothes to bring. The night before, I pack my bag. I always bring a portable charger, some medicine, and comfortable shoes. And I always check my passport twice, because I once almost forgot it on the way to the airport. That was a nightmare. That’s how I usually prepare for a trip.",
"travel:2":"On my last trip to Japan, I had a big problem. I lost my wallet on the second day. We had taken a taxi from a restaurant back to the hotel, and when I got to my room, I realized my wallet was gone. I think I left it in the taxi. I was really panicked at first, because my cash, my credit cards, and even my driver’s license were all in it. I didn’t know what to do, and I couldn’t speak Japanese at all. My friend calmed me down, and we made a plan. First, I called my card company and canceled my credit cards, so no one could use them. Then we went to the police station near the hotel. I explained the situation in simple English and showed them the taxi receipt, which luckily I had in my pocket. The police officer was very kind, and he called the taxi company for us. Luckily, the taxi driver found my wallet and brought it back to the police station the next day. Nothing was missing. I was so relieved and grateful. I learned an important lesson from that experience. Since then, I always keep some cash and a spare card in a separate place when I travel.",

"jogging:0":"I usually jog along the river near my house. It’s about ten minutes on foot from my apartment, so it’s really easy to get there. There’s a long path just for walking and running, and there’s a separate lane for bikes, so it’s pretty safe. The path is flat and wide, and it goes on for many kilometers. On one side, you can see the river, and on the other side, there are trees, grass, and flowers. There are also benches, restrooms, water fountains, and convenience stores along the way, so it’s very convenient. The view is really nice, especially at night when the bridges light up with different colors. It looks really romantic. In the evening, the path is full of people jogging, walking their dogs, or riding bikes. Some people even have picnics on the grass. In the spring and fall, the weather is perfect for running, so it gets really crowded. In the summer, it’s a little too hot during the day, so most people come out at night. I think it’s the perfect place to exercise in the city. Whenever I run there, I feel free and energized, and all my stress just goes away. That’s where I usually jog.",
"jogging:1":"I jog three times a week, usually on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, after work around eight. Before I leave home, I change into my running clothes and put on my running shoes. I bring my phone, earbuds, and a small water bottle. When I get to the river, I always stretch for five minutes first, so I don’t get hurt. I once hurt my ankle because I skipped stretching, so now I never skip it. Then I start by walking slowly for about five minutes to warm up. After that, I run about five kilometers. It takes about thirty minutes. I use an app to check my time and distance, and it’s fun to see my record get better every month. While I run, I listen to fast music with a strong beat, because it helps me keep my pace. When I get tired, I slow down a little, but I try not to stop. After jogging, I walk for ten minutes to cool down and drink some water. Then I go home and take a shower. I always sleep really well on those days. On weekends, I sometimes run a longer distance, like ten kilometers. It’s hard, but I feel great afterward. That’s my jogging routine.",
"jogging:2":"I still remember one evening last summer. I went jogging along the river as usual after work. The weather was fine when I left home. It was a little cloudy, but I didn’t think it would rain, so I didn’t bring an umbrella. But about twenty minutes later, the sky suddenly got really dark, and it started raining really hard. It was like someone was pouring water from a bucket. I got completely soaked in seconds. Even my phone and earbuds got wet, and I was worried they might break. I ran under a bridge as fast as I could and waited there with a lot of other people. Everyone was soaked, and we all looked so silly that we started laughing. A woman next to me even shared her towel with me. We waited for about thirty minutes, and we chatted about the weather and jogging. Finally, the rain stopped, and I jogged home in wet clothes. My shoes were full of water, so every step made a funny sound. It was a little uncomfortable, and I caught a small cold. But honestly, it was funny, and now it’s a good memory. Since then, I always check the weather app before I go jogging.",

"cafe:0":"There’s a small café I like near my office. It’s on the second floor of an old building, so it’s a little hard to find, but that’s what makes it special. When you walk in, it has a warm and cozy atmosphere. The walls are white, the floor is made of wood, and there are lots of plants by the windows. The lights are soft and yellow, and they usually play soft jazz music. There are only about ten tables, so it’s never too loud, and people usually talk quietly or work on their laptops. There’s also a big window seat where you can see the street below. That’s my favorite seat. Their coffee is really strong and smooth. The owner roasts the beans himself, and you can smell the coffee from the stairs. Their cheesecake is the best I’ve ever had. It’s not too sweet, and it goes perfectly with an Americano. The owner is also really friendly, and he remembers my usual order. I like it because I can relax there and forget about work for a while. Compared to big chain cafés, it feels much more personal. I go there at least twice a week. That’s my favorite café.",
"cafe:1":"I go to cafés quite often, maybe four or five times a week. On weekdays, I usually go to a café during my lunch break with my coworkers. After lunch, we walk to a café near our office. I always order an iced Americano, even in winter. My coworkers usually get lattes or tea. We chat about everyday things, like movies, food, our families, or our weekend plans. Sometimes we complain about work, too. It’s a nice way to take a break and get to know each other better. We usually stay there for about twenty minutes and then go back to the office. On weekends, it’s different. I go to a café near my house by myself. I bring my laptop and study English for a couple of hours. I find it easier to focus in a café than at home, because at home I just want to lie down. Sometimes I read a book or listen to music instead. And once or twice a month, I meet my old friends at a nice café, and we talk for hours. For me, a café is not just a place to drink coffee. It’s a place to relax, focus, and recharge. That’s what I usually do at cafés.",
"cafe:2":"Something unexpected happened at a café last year. I was at a café near my office, waiting for my coffee. I had an important meeting with a client in about twenty minutes, so I was wearing my best white shirt. When the barista was bringing my drink, she slipped on the wet floor, and she spilled coffee all over my shirt. Luckily, it wasn’t too hot, so I didn’t get burned. But my shirt was completely ruined. The barista was so shocked, and she apologized many times. The manager came out, too, and gave me a free drink and a gift card. I wasn’t really angry, because it was clearly an accident. But I was really worried about the meeting. I didn’t know what to do at first. Then I remembered there was a clothing store nearby. So I ran to the store, quickly bought a new shirt, and changed in the fitting room. I made it to the meeting just in time, and it went really well. Funny enough, now I’m a regular at that café, and the barista and I always say hi to each other. She even remembers my order. It was a stressful day, but now it’s a funny story.",

"roleplay:0":"Hi, I’m calling to ask about this weekend’s movies. I’d like to see a movie with my friend on Saturday, and I have a few questions. First, what movies are playing on Saturday? Is there a good action movie or a comedy? Oh, I see. That new action movie sounds great. I’ve heard a lot of good things about it. What time does it start? Are there any shows in the evening? Eight thirty? Perfect, that works for us. And how long is the movie? Two hours? Okay, that’s fine. Next, how much is a ticket for adults? I see. Is there a discount if I book online or pay with a certain credit card? Oh, really? That’s good to know. I’ll book online, then. Also, are there still good seats available? We’d like to sit in the middle. Great. One more thing, is there a parking lot in the building? And is parking free if we watch a movie? Oh, three hours free. That’s perfect. Lastly, can we bring our own snacks, or do we have to buy them there? Okay, I understand. Thank you so much for your help. You’ve been really helpful. Have a nice day.",
"roleplay:1":"Excuse me, I’m staying in room twelve oh five, and I’m sorry to bother you, but I have a problem with my room. When I checked in about an hour ago, everything seemed fine. But when I tried to turn on the air conditioner, it didn’t work at all. I tried turning it on and off several times, and I also checked the remote control and changed the batteries, but nothing happened. It’s really hot and humid tonight, and the window doesn’t open very much, so it’s too hot to sleep. Also, I have an early meeting tomorrow morning, so I really need a good night’s sleep. So I’d like to suggest a few options. First, could you send someone to fix it right now? If it can be fixed in thirty minutes, I can wait. If that’s not possible, can I change to another room? I don’t mind a smaller room, as long as the air conditioner works. Or if there are no rooms available tonight, I’d appreciate it if you could give me a discount, and maybe bring me a fan. I’m sure you can understand my situation. Please let me know what you can do. Thank you for your help.",
"roleplay:2":"Hey, it’s me. How are you doing? Thanks for inviting me to your party on Friday. I was really looking forward to it, and I already bought a small gift for you. But I’m so sorry, I can’t make it. I just found out this morning that I have to work late that day. My team has an important project, and the deadline is Monday, so my boss asked everyone to stay late on Friday. I tried to get out of it, but there was no way. I feel really bad, because I know you’ve been planning this party for weeks. So I have a couple of ideas. How about having dinner next weekend instead? There’s a new Italian restaurant near my office, and I heard the pasta there is really good. I’ll treat you to make it up to you. If you’re busy next weekend, we could meet on a weekday evening instead. Or maybe I could stop by your place on Saturday to give you your gift. Let me know what day works for you, and I’ll make a reservation. Anyway, I hope you have a great time at the party. Say hi to everyone for me, and send me some pictures. Talk to you soon.",

"surprise:0":"In Korea, most people use the subway and buses, especially in big cities like Seoul. Public transportation is fast, cheap, and clean, and it runs until about midnight. The subway is especially popular, because it’s never stuck in traffic. In Seoul, there are more than twenty subway lines, so you can go almost anywhere. You can use one card for both the subway and buses, and you get a discount when you transfer within thirty minutes. Many people also use taxis, especially late at night, and these days, people call taxis with an app. Compared to the past, public transportation has changed a lot. When I was a kid, people had to pay with cash or paper tickets, and the buses were often late and crowded. There was no way to know when the bus would come, so you just had to wait. Now you can check the exact bus arrival time on your phone, and many bus stops have screens, too. The buses are also much cleaner and quieter now, and some of them are electric. Personally, I take the subway to work every day. It’s not perfect, because it’s really crowded during rush hour. But overall, I think Korea has one of the best public transportation systems in the world.",
"surprise:1":"Korea has a very strict recycling system. People have to separate their trash into many different types. We separate plastic, paper, cans, glass, and vinyl, and we have to rinse the containers before we throw them away. For example, if you throw away a plastic bottle, you have to take off the label and wash it first. Food waste goes in a separate bin, and in many apartments, you pay for it by weight with a card. General trash must go in special plastic bags that you have to buy at the supermarket. If you don’t follow the rules, you can get a fine. At first, it was confusing for a lot of people, but now most people are used to it. At home, I keep a few boxes on the balcony for each type of recycling. My family shares the work. My mom takes care of the food waste, and I take care of the recycling. In my apartment, recycling day is every Wednesday, so I take everything down in the evening. It takes about ten minutes. Compared to the past, people recycle much more now. When I was young, people just threw everything away together. It’s a little annoying sometimes, but I think it’s really good for the environment, and I’m glad we do it.",
"surprise:2":"Almost everyone in Korea uses a smartphone, from kids to grandparents. I think it’s the technology that has changed people’s lives the most. We use it for everything, like banking, shopping, ordering food, booking movie tickets, and even paying at stores. For example, I don’t carry a wallet anymore, because I pay with my phone. I also use it to check the bus arrival time, find restaurants, and talk to my family. When I was in high school, I had a simple phone that could only make calls and send text messages. I got my first smartphone in college, and my life changed a lot. Now I can’t imagine a day without it. I think it has made our lives much more convenient and faster. On the other hand, there are some problems, too. People talk to each other less, even when they’re at the same table. Many people spend too much time on their phones, and some kids are addicted to games and videos. On the subway, almost everyone is looking at a screen. Also, older people sometimes have trouble using apps, so they feel left behind. So personally, I try to use my phone less. I don’t use it before bed, and I put it away when I’m with my family.",
"surprise:3":"One of the biggest holidays in Korea is Chuseok. It’s like Thanksgiving in America. It’s a harvest festival, and it usually lasts three days in the fall, around September or October. On Chuseok, families get together at their parents’ or grandparents’ house. Many people live far from their hometown, so they travel a long way to see their families. Because everyone travels at the same time, the roads are always packed with traffic. Sometimes a trip that normally takes four hours takes eight or nine hours. On Chuseok, we make and eat a lot of traditional food. The most famous one is songpyeon, a kind of half-moon-shaped rice cake. The whole family sits together and makes it by hand. We also make different kinds of pancakes, called jeon. Many families also hold a memorial service for their ancestors in the morning and visit their graves to show respect. In the evening, people look at the full moon and make a wish. Compared to the past, Chuseok has changed a little. These days, some families just go on a trip together instead of cooking all day. My family still meets at my grandmother’s house. It’s a little tiring, but it’s a special time to catch up with family, so I always look forward to it."
};

// 주제별 추가 문항. t: 묘사 / 비교(과거와 지금) / 경험. s는 짧은 답안(IM 목표), m은 2분 답안(IH 목표).
const MORE = {
home:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Tell me about your favorite room in your home. What does it look like, and what do you usually do there?", ko:"집에서 가장 좋아하는 방에 대해 말해 주세요. 어떻게 생겼고 거기서 주로 무엇을 하나요?",
  k:[["My favorite room in my home is my bedroom.","집에서 가장 좋아하는 방은 제 침실이에요."],
     ["It’s small, but it has everything I need.","작지만 필요한 건 다 있어요."],
     ["Next to the window, there’s a desk where I study.","창가 옆에 공부하는 책상이 있어요."],
     ["I spend most of my free time there.","여가 시간 대부분을 거기서 보내요."],
     ["It’s the only place where I can be alone.","혼자 있을 수 있는 유일한 곳이에요."]],
  s:"My favorite room in my home is my bedroom. It’s small, but it has everything I need. There’s a bed, a closet, and a bookshelf. Next to the window, there’s a desk where I study and use my laptop. I put some small plants and photos on the desk, so it feels cozy. I spend most of my free time there. I watch videos, read books, and listen to music. It’s the only place where I can be alone and relax, so I really love it.",
  m:"My favorite room in my home is definitely my bedroom. It’s not very big, but it has everything I need. When you open the door, you can see my bed on the left side. I have a big, soft blanket that I bought last winter, and it’s really comfortable. On the right side, there’s a closet and a tall bookshelf full of books and comic books. Next to the window, there’s a desk where I study and use my laptop. I put some small plants and photos of my friends on the desk, so it feels warm and cozy. The window faces east, so I get a lot of sunlight in the morning. I spend most of my free time there. On weekdays, I usually watch videos or study English at my desk. On weekends, I lie on my bed and read a book or listen to music for hours. Sometimes I just take a nap. Compared to the living room, it’s much quieter, because the TV is always on in the living room. Honestly, it’s the only place where I can be alone and really relax. That’s why it’s my favorite room."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How is the home you live in now different from the home you lived in when you were a child?", ko:"지금 사는 집은 어릴 때 살던 집과 어떻게 다른가요?",
  k:[["When I was a child, I lived in a small house with a yard.","어릴 때는 마당이 있는 작은 주택에 살았어요."],
     ["Now I live in an apartment in the city.","지금은 도시의 아파트에 살아요."],
     ["My old house was cold in winter.","예전 집은 겨울에 추웠어요."],
     ["My apartment is much more convenient.","지금 아파트가 훨씬 편해요."],
     ["Sometimes I miss playing in the yard.","가끔 마당에서 놀던 게 그리워요."]],
  s:"When I was a child, I lived in a small house with a yard in my hometown. Now I live in an apartment in the city. My old house was old, and it was really cold in winter. My apartment is much newer and warmer, and it’s close to the subway station. So it’s much more convenient. But my old house had a yard, and I used to play there with my dog. Sometimes I really miss that.",
  m:"The home I live in now is really different from the home I lived in when I was a child. When I was a child, I lived in a small house with a yard in my hometown, a small city in the countryside. The house was about thirty years old. It had two bedrooms, a small kitchen, and a yard where my mom grew vegetables. I used to play there with my dog every day after school. In summer, we sometimes had barbecues in the yard with our neighbors. But the house was really cold in winter, because the heating wasn’t very good. Now I live in an apartment in the city. It’s much newer, and it’s warm in winter and cool in summer. It’s also close to the subway station and a big supermarket, so it’s much more convenient. There’s a security guard, too, so it feels safe. On the other hand, my apartment doesn’t have a yard, and I don’t really know my neighbors. In my old neighborhood, everyone knew each other. So I think my life is more convenient now, but sometimes I really miss my old house and the yard. That’s the biggest difference."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a time you had a problem at home, such as something breaking. What happened, and how did you solve it?", ko:"집에서 무언가 고장 나는 등 문제가 생겼던 경험을 말해 주세요. 무슨 일이었고 어떻게 해결했나요?",
  k:[["Last winter, the boiler in my apartment broke.","작년 겨울에 아파트 보일러가 고장 났어요."],
     ["There was no hot water, and the house was freezing.","온수가 안 나오고 집이 꽁꽁 얼었어요."],
     ["I called a repairman right away.","바로 수리 기사님을 불렀어요."],
     ["He couldn’t come until the next day.","그분이 다음 날에야 올 수 있었어요."],
     ["Since then, I check the boiler every fall.","그 뒤로 매년 가을 보일러를 점검해요."]],
  s:"Last winter, the boiler in my apartment broke. It was really cold outside, and there was no hot water, so the house was freezing. I called a repairman right away, but he couldn’t come until the next day. So my family wore thick clothes and used an electric blanket that night. The next morning, the repairman came and fixed it in an hour. It was a really hard night. Since then, I check the boiler every fall.",
  m:"I still remember a problem I had at home last winter. It was the coldest week of the year, and one night, the boiler in my apartment suddenly broke. At first, I didn’t notice, but then I realized the floor was getting cold. When I tried to take a shower, there was no hot water at all. The house was freezing, and I was really worried because my parents were at home, too. I called a repairman right away, but it was already late at night, so he couldn’t come until the next day. I didn’t know what to do at first. So my family wore thick clothes and socks, and we all slept in one room with an electric blanket. We also boiled water in the kitchen so we could wash our faces. It was actually kind of funny, like camping at home. The next morning, the repairman came and found that one small part was broken. He fixed it in about an hour. I was so relieved when the hot water came back. It was a hard night, but I learned something. Since then, I always check the boiler every fall before winter starts. That’s what happened."}],
neighborhood:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Describe the people in your neighborhood. What are your neighbors like, and how do you get along with them?", ko:"동네 사람들을 묘사해 주세요. 이웃들은 어떤 사람들이고 어떻게 지내나요?",
  k:[["Most of my neighbors are young families with kids.","이웃 대부분은 아이가 있는 젊은 가족이에요."],
     ["We usually just say hello in the elevator.","보통 엘리베이터에서 인사만 해요."],
     ["The lady next door is really kind.","옆집 아주머니가 정말 친절해요."],
     ["She sometimes shares food with my family.","가끔 우리 가족에게 음식을 나눠 주세요."],
     ["I think my neighbors are friendly but busy.","이웃들은 친절하지만 바쁜 것 같아요."]],
  s:"Most of my neighbors are young families with kids, and there are some older people, too. Everyone is pretty busy, so we usually just say hello in the elevator. But the lady next door is really kind. She sometimes shares food with my family, like kimchi or rice cakes. When we go on a trip, she takes care of our packages. I think my neighbors are friendly but busy. I’m happy to live near nice people.",
  m:"I live in an apartment building, so I have a lot of neighbors. Most of them are young families with kids, and there are also some older couples and a few people who live alone. In the morning, you can see parents taking their kids to school, and in the evening, kids play in the playground in front of the building. Honestly, everyone is pretty busy, so we don’t talk much. We usually just say hello in the elevator or chat a little about the weather. But there’s one neighbor I know well. The lady next door is really kind. She’s in her sixties, and she lives with her husband. She sometimes shares food with my family, like kimchi, rice cakes, or fruit from her hometown. In return, my mom gives her some side dishes. When we go on a trip, she takes care of our packages, and she even waters our plants. Compared to the past, people don’t know their neighbors very well these days. When I was young, everyone in my neighborhood knew each other. But I still think my neighbors are friendly. They’re quiet and polite, and there are no noise problems. I’m happy to live near nice people. That’s what my neighbors are like."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How has your neighborhood changed since you first moved there? What was it like before, and what is it like now?", ko:"처음 이사 왔을 때와 비교해 동네가 어떻게 바뀌었나요? 예전엔 어땠고 지금은 어떤가요?",
  k:[["When I first moved here, there wasn’t much around.","처음 이사 왔을 땐 주변에 별게 없었어요."],
     ["There used to be a lot of empty land.","예전엔 빈 땅이 많았어요."],
     ["Now there are new apartments and shopping malls.","지금은 새 아파트와 쇼핑몰이 생겼어요."],
     ["A new subway station opened two years ago.","2년 전에 지하철역이 새로 생겼어요."],
     ["It’s more convenient, but it’s also more crowded.","더 편해졌지만 더 붐비기도 해요."]],
  s:"When I first moved here about five years ago, there wasn’t much around. There used to be a lot of empty land, and I had to take a bus to go shopping. But now there are new apartments, a big shopping mall, and lots of restaurants. A new subway station opened two years ago, too. So it’s much more convenient now. But it’s also more crowded and noisy. I liked the quiet, but I’m happy with the changes.",
  m:"My neighborhood has changed a lot since I first moved here about five years ago. When I first moved here, there wasn’t much around. There used to be a lot of empty land and some old houses, and it was really quiet at night. There was only one small supermarket, so I had to take a bus for twenty minutes to go shopping or to see a movie. Also, the nearest subway station was far, so getting to work took almost an hour. But now it’s a completely different place. There are new apartments, a big shopping mall, and lots of restaurants and cafés. A new subway station opened right near my apartment two years ago, so now it only takes thirty minutes to get to work. There’s also a new library and a park, which I really like. On the other hand, there are some downsides, too. The neighborhood is much more crowded and noisy now, and traffic is bad during rush hour. Also, housing prices have gone up a lot. Honestly, I sometimes miss how quiet it used to be. But overall, I’m happy with the changes, because my life is much more convenient now. That’s how my neighborhood has changed."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a time when you helped a neighbor, or a neighbor helped you. What happened?", ko:"이웃을 도왔거나 이웃이 나를 도와준 경험을 말해 주세요. 무슨 일이 있었나요?",
  k:[["One day, I locked myself out of my apartment.","어느 날 집 열쇠 없이 문이 잠겨 버렸어요."],
     ["My phone was inside, so I couldn’t call anyone.","휴대폰이 안에 있어서 아무에게도 전화를 못 했어요."],
     ["My neighbor let me use her phone.","이웃이 휴대폰을 빌려줬어요."],
     ["She even invited me in for a cup of tea.","차 한잔하라고 집에 들어오라고까지 했어요."],
     ["I gave her a small gift to thank her.","감사의 뜻으로 작은 선물을 드렸어요."]],
  s:"One day last year, I locked myself out of my apartment. My phone was inside, so I couldn’t call anyone. I didn’t know what to do. Then my neighbor came out and asked if I was okay. She let me use her phone, so I called a locksmith. She even invited me in for a cup of tea while I waited. The next day, I gave her a small gift to thank her. Now we’re good friends.",
  m:"I still remember the time a neighbor helped me last year. It was a Sunday morning, and I went out to take out the trash. I was wearing pajamas and slippers, and I didn’t bring anything with me. When I came back, I realized the door had locked behind me. My key and my phone were both inside, so I couldn’t call anyone. I was really embarrassed and didn’t know what to do. I just stood in the hallway for a few minutes. Then the lady next door came out and asked if I was okay. I explained the situation, and she laughed and said the same thing had happened to her before. She let me use her phone, so I called a locksmith. He said he would come in about an hour. Then she invited me in for a cup of tea while I waited. We talked about our families, our jobs, and the neighborhood. I found out she used to be an English teacher. Finally, the locksmith came and opened my door. The next day, I gave her a small cake to thank her. Since then, we’ve become good friends, and we often chat. It was embarrassing, but it turned out to be a good experience."}],
movies:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Tell me about the movie theater you usually go to. Where is it, and what is it like?", ko:"주로 가는 영화관에 대해 말해 주세요. 어디에 있고 어떤 곳인가요?",
  k:[["The theater I usually go to is in a shopping mall.","주로 가는 영화관은 쇼핑몰 안에 있어요."],
     ["It’s about fifteen minutes from my house by bus.","집에서 버스로 15분쯤 걸려요."],
     ["It has ten screens and very comfortable seats.","상영관이 10개 있고 좌석이 아주 편해요."],
     ["There’s a big snack bar in the lobby.","로비에 큰 매점이 있어요."],
     ["It’s always crowded on weekends.","주말엔 항상 붐벼요."]],
  s:"The theater I usually go to is in a shopping mall near my house. It’s about fifteen minutes by bus. It has ten screens and very comfortable seats. Some seats even lie back like a bed. There’s a big snack bar in the lobby, and it smells like popcorn. It’s always crowded on weekends, so I usually book my ticket early. I like it because I can eat and shop before the movie.",
  m:"The movie theater I usually go to is in a big shopping mall near my house. It’s about fifteen minutes by bus, so it’s pretty easy to get there. The theater is on the top floor of the mall. When you get off the elevator, you can see a big lobby with lots of movie posters and screens showing trailers. There’s a big snack bar in the middle, and the whole place smells like popcorn. There are also some self-service machines, so you can print your tickets quickly. The theater has ten screens, and the seats are really comfortable. They’re wide and soft, and some of them even lie back like a bed. My favorite is the IMAX screen. It’s huge, and the sound is amazing, so action movies look really exciting there. It’s a little more expensive, but it’s worth it. The theater is always crowded on weekends, especially with families and couples, so I usually book my ticket a few days early. I like this theater because it’s convenient. Before the movie, I can have dinner at a restaurant in the mall, and after the movie, I can do some shopping. That’s the theater I usually go to."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How has the way people watch movies changed compared to the past?", ko:"사람들이 영화를 보는 방식은 예전과 비교해 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["In the past, people had to go to a theater or rent a DVD.","예전엔 영화관에 가거나 DVD를 빌려야 했어요."],
     ["These days, most people watch movies on streaming apps.","요즘은 대부분 스트리밍 앱으로 영화를 봐요."],
     ["You can watch a movie anytime, anywhere.","언제 어디서나 영화를 볼 수 있어요."],
     ["Movie tickets have become much more expensive.","영화표가 훨씬 비싸졌어요."],
     ["I think theaters are still special, though.","그래도 영화관은 여전히 특별한 것 같아요."]],
  s:"The way people watch movies has changed a lot. In the past, people had to go to a theater or rent a DVD from a video store. These days, most people watch movies on streaming apps like Netflix. You can watch a movie anytime, anywhere, even on the subway. Also, movie tickets have become much more expensive. So people go to theaters less often. I think theaters are still special, though.",
  m:"The way people watch movies has changed a lot compared to the past. When I was a kid, there were only two choices. You could go to a theater, or you could rent a video or a DVD from a video store. I remember going to a small video store near my house with my dad every Friday. We had to return the DVD in two days, or we had to pay a late fee. Also, we had to wait for months for a new movie to come out on DVD. These days, things are totally different. Most people watch movies on streaming apps like Netflix or Disney Plus. You can watch a movie anytime, anywhere, even on your phone on the subway. New movies come out on streaming apps just a few weeks after they’re in theaters. Also, movie tickets have become much more expensive. They’re about fifteen thousand won now. So people go to theaters less often, and they only go for big movies. Personally, I watch most movies at home now, because it’s cheap and convenient. But I think theaters are still special, though. Watching a big action movie on a huge screen with great sound is a totally different experience. That’s how it has changed."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a time something unexpected or funny happened while you were watching a movie.", ko:"영화를 보다가 뜻밖이거나 웃긴 일이 있었던 경험을 말해 주세요.",
  k:[["One time, I fell asleep in the middle of a movie.","한번은 영화 중간에 잠들어 버렸어요."],
     ["I was really tired after working late.","야근 후라 정말 피곤했어요."],
     ["When I woke up, the movie was already over.","깨어 보니 영화가 이미 끝나 있었어요."],
     ["My friend was laughing at me.","친구가 저를 보며 웃고 있었어요."],
     ["Now I never go to late-night movies.","이제 심야 영화는 절대 안 봐요."]],
  s:"One time, I fell asleep in the middle of a movie. I went to a late-night movie with my friend after working late, and I was really tired. The seats were so comfortable that I fell asleep in twenty minutes. When I woke up, the movie was already over, and my friend was laughing at me. I even snored a little. It was so embarrassing. Now I never go to late-night movies.",
  m:"I still remember a really funny thing that happened about a year ago. My friend and I went to see a new action movie. We had been waiting for it for months, so we were really excited. But that day, I had worked late, and I was really tired. We bought the last show, which started at eleven at night. We got popcorn and sat in these really comfortable seats that lie back. The movie started, and the first scene was really exciting. But after about twenty minutes, I started to feel sleepy. I tried really hard to stay awake. I drank my Coke and ate some popcorn, but it didn’t help. The next thing I knew, the lights were on, and the movie was already over. My friend was laughing at me. He said I fell asleep for almost two hours, and I even snored a little during a quiet scene. The people next to us heard it, too. It was so embarrassing. I had to ask my friend what happened in the movie on the way home. In the end, I watched it again the next weekend. Now I never go to late-night movies when I’m tired. That’s the funny story."}],
music:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Describe your favorite singer or band. What kind of music do they make, and why do you like them?", ko:"좋아하는 가수나 밴드를 묘사해 주세요. 어떤 음악을 하고 왜 좋아하나요?",
  k:[["My favorite band is a Korean rock band called Day6.","가장 좋아하는 밴드는 데이식스라는 한국 록 밴드예요."],
     ["They write and play their own songs.","직접 곡을 쓰고 연주해요."],
     ["Their songs are about love and everyday life.","노래가 사랑과 일상에 관한 내용이에요."],
     ["Their lyrics really touch my heart.","가사가 정말 마음에 와닿아요."],
     ["Their music gives me a lot of energy.","그들의 음악은 저에게 힘을 많이 줘요."]],
  s:"My favorite band is a Korean rock band called Day6. There are four members, and they write and play their own songs. Their music is a mix of rock and pop, so it’s easy to listen to. Their songs are about love, friendship, and everyday life. Their lyrics really touch my heart, especially when I’m having a hard time. Their music gives me a lot of energy. I listen to them every day.",
  m:"My favorite band is a Korean rock band called Day6. There are four members, and they play guitar, bass, keyboard, and drums. What I like most about them is that they write and play their own songs. A lot of K-pop groups focus on dancing, but Day6 really focuses on the music itself. Their music is a mix of rock and pop, so it’s exciting but also easy to listen to. Their songs are mostly about love, friendship, and everyday life. For example, some songs are about growing up, and some are about missing someone. Their lyrics really touch my heart, especially when I’m having a hard time at work. It feels like they understand how I feel. My favorite song is called You Were Beautiful. It’s a sad song, but it’s really beautiful. I first heard it about five years ago, and I’ve been a fan since then. Last year, I went to their concert, and they were even better live. Everyone sang along, and it was amazing. Their music gives me a lot of energy and comfort. I listen to them every day on my way to work. That’s why they’re my favorite band."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How has the way people listen to music changed over the years?", ko:"사람들이 음악을 듣는 방식은 세월에 따라 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["When I was young, people listened to CDs and the radio.","어릴 땐 사람들이 CD와 라디오로 들었어요."],
     ["Then MP3 players became really popular.","그다음 MP3 플레이어가 크게 유행했어요."],
     ["Now everyone uses streaming apps on their phones.","지금은 모두 휴대폰 스트리밍 앱을 써요."],
     ["The app recommends songs for you.","앱이 노래를 추천해 줘요."],
     ["People don’t buy albums as much as before.","예전만큼 앨범을 사지 않아요."]],
  s:"The way people listen to music has changed a lot. When I was young, people listened to CDs and the radio. Then MP3 players became really popular, and we downloaded songs on the computer. Now everyone uses streaming apps on their phones. You can listen to any song you want, and the app even recommends songs for you. It’s very convenient. But people don’t buy albums as much as before, except for K-pop fans.",
  m:"The way people listen to music has changed a lot over the years. When I was a kid, people mostly listened to music on the radio or on CDs. I remember my parents had a big stereo in the living room, and my dad had a lot of CDs. If you wanted a new song, you had to go to a music store and buy the whole album. Then, when I was in middle school, MP3 players became really popular. We downloaded songs on the computer and put them on our MP3 players. I could only carry about two hundred songs, so I had to choose carefully. Now everything is different. Everyone uses streaming apps on their phones, like Melon or Spotify. You pay a monthly fee, and you can listen to millions of songs anytime, anywhere. The app even recommends songs for you based on what you like, so it’s easy to find new music. Also, people use wireless earbuds now, so it’s much more convenient. On the other hand, people don’t buy albums as much as before, except for K-pop fans who collect them. Personally, I think streaming is great, but I sometimes miss the feeling of buying a new CD and reading the lyrics booklet. That’s how it has changed."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a concert or live performance you went to. What was memorable about it?", ko:"가 본 콘서트나 공연에 대해 말해 주세요. 무엇이 기억에 남나요?",
  k:[["A few years ago, I went to an outdoor music festival.","몇 년 전에 야외 음악 축제에 갔어요."],
     ["It was held in a big park by the river.","강변의 큰 공원에서 열렸어요."],
     ["Thousands of people were singing and dancing.","수천 명이 노래하고 춤췄어요."],
     ["Suddenly, it started to rain during the show.","공연 중에 갑자기 비가 오기 시작했어요."],
     ["Nobody left, and it became even more exciting.","아무도 안 떠났고 오히려 더 신났어요."]],
  s:"A few years ago, I went to an outdoor music festival with my friends. It was held in a big park by the river. There were a lot of famous singers and bands. Thousands of people were singing and dancing together. Suddenly, it started to rain during the show. But nobody left. We just kept dancing in the rain, and it became even more exciting. It was the best concert I’ve ever been to.",
  m:"The most memorable concert I’ve been to was an outdoor music festival about three years ago. It was held in a big park by the river in Seoul, and it lasted two days. I went on the second day with two of my close friends. We bought the tickets two months early, because they sold out really fast. There were a lot of famous singers and bands, and my favorite band was the last performer of the day. When we got there in the afternoon, the park was already full of people. Everyone was sitting on mats, eating food, and enjoying the music. In the evening, thousands of people were standing in front of the stage, singing and dancing together. Then, something unexpected happened. Suddenly, it started to rain really hard during my favorite band’s show. At first, I was disappointed, because I didn’t bring a raincoat. But nobody left. The singer said, ‘Let’s enjoy the rain together,’ and everyone screamed. We just kept dancing in the rain, and it became even more exciting. We were completely soaked, but we didn’t care. It felt like a scene from a movie. It was the best concert I’ve ever been to, and I still talk about it with my friends."}],
park:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"What do people in your country usually do at parks? Describe what you can see at a typical park.", ko:"당신 나라 사람들은 공원에서 보통 무엇을 하나요? 흔한 공원의 모습을 묘사해 주세요.",
  k:[["Parks in Korea are always full of people.","한국의 공원은 항상 사람들로 가득해요."],
     ["Many people walk or jog in the evening.","많은 사람이 저녁에 걷거나 뛰어요."],
     ["Older people often use the exercise machines.","어르신들은 운동 기구를 자주 이용해요."],
     ["Families have picnics on the weekends.","가족들은 주말에 소풍을 해요."],
     ["Some people order fried chicken to the park.","공원으로 치킨을 배달시키는 사람도 있어요."]],
  s:"Parks in Korea are always full of people, especially in the evening and on weekends. Many people walk or jog around the park after work. Older people often use the exercise machines. On weekends, families have picnics on the grass, and kids ride bikes or play in the playground. Some people even order fried chicken to the park. Parks are a great place for people to relax in the city.",
  m:"In Korea, parks are really important, because most people live in apartments and don’t have their own yards. So parks are always full of people, especially in the evening and on weekends. At a typical park, you can see a walking trail, some trees and benches, a playground, and outdoor exercise machines. In the morning, older people come to the park to walk or use the exercise machines. Some of them even do group exercises together, like stretching or dancing. In the evening, after work, many people walk or jog around the park. You can also see a lot of people walking their dogs. On weekends, it’s even busier. Families have picnics on the grass, and kids ride bikes, fly kites, or play in the playground. Young couples sit on mats and take pictures. One interesting thing about Korean parks is food delivery. Some people order fried chicken or jajangmyeon to the park, and the delivery driver finds them on the grass. Foreigners are often surprised by that. In big parks along the river, there are also concerts and festivals in the summer. I think parks are a great place for people to relax and spend time together in the city."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How are parks today different from the parks you remember from when you were young?", ko:"요즘 공원은 어렸을 때 기억하는 공원과 어떻게 다른가요?",
  k:[["When I was young, parks were small and simple.","어릴 땐 공원이 작고 단순했어요."],
     ["There was just a slide and a few swings.","미끄럼틀과 그네 몇 개만 있었어요."],
     ["Now parks are much bigger and cleaner.","지금 공원은 훨씬 크고 깨끗해요."],
     ["There are walking trails, fountains, and even cafés.","산책로, 분수, 카페까지 있어요."],
     ["Kids today don’t play outside as much.","요즘 아이들은 밖에서 덜 놀아요."]],
  s:"When I was young, parks were small and simple. There was just a slide, a few swings, and a sandbox. Now parks are much bigger and cleaner. There are walking trails, fountains, exercise machines, and even cafés. Many parks also have CCTV, so they’re safer. But I think kids today don’t play outside as much as we did, because they play games on their phones. That’s a little sad.",
  m:"Parks today are really different from the parks I remember from when I was young. When I was a kid, the park near my house was small and simple. There was just a slide, a few swings, a sandbox, and some old benches. There weren’t many trees, and in the summer, it was really hot. At night, it was dark and a little scary, so we never went there after dinner. But my friends and I played there every day after school until our moms called us home for dinner. Now parks are much bigger, cleaner, and nicer. There are long walking trails, lots of trees and flowers, fountains, and outdoor exercise machines. Some big parks even have cafés, libraries, and stages for concerts. They also have bright lights and CCTV, so they’re safe even at night. That’s why so many people go walking after dinner now. On the other hand, I think kids today don’t play outside as much as we did. When I go to the park, I see more adults exercising than kids playing. Many kids are busy with academies, or they play games on their phones. That’s a little sad. Overall, parks have gotten much better, but the way people use them has changed, too."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a special day you spent at a park with your family or friends.", ko:"가족이나 친구와 공원에서 보낸 특별한 하루에 대해 말해 주세요.",
  k:[["Last spring, my family had a picnic at a park.","작년 봄에 가족과 공원에서 소풍을 했어요."],
     ["It was my mom’s sixtieth birthday.","엄마의 환갑이었어요."],
     ["We prepared kimbap and a birthday cake.","김밥과 생일 케이크를 준비했어요."],
     ["The cherry blossoms were in full bloom.","벚꽃이 활짝 피어 있었어요."],
     ["My mom said it was her best birthday ever.","엄마가 최고의 생일이었다고 하셨어요."]],
  s:"Last spring, my family had a special picnic at a park. It was my mom’s sixtieth birthday. Instead of going to a fancy restaurant, we decided to have a picnic, because my mom loves flowers. We prepared kimbap, fruit, and a birthday cake. The cherry blossoms were in full bloom, and it was really beautiful. We took a lot of pictures and sang happy birthday. My mom said it was her best birthday ever.",
  m:"I still remember a special day I spent at a park last spring. It was my mom’s sixtieth birthday, which is a really important birthday in Korea. At first, we planned to go to a fancy restaurant. But my mom said she wanted something simple, and she loves flowers. So my brother and I decided to surprise her with a picnic at a big park near the river. The night before, we prepared everything. We made kimbap and fried chicken, cut some fruit, and ordered a small birthday cake. In the morning, we told my mom we were just going for a walk. When we got to the park, the cherry blossoms were in full bloom, and the whole park was pink and white. It was really beautiful. We found a nice spot under a big tree, laid out a mat, and set up the food. When my mom saw everything, she was really surprised and almost cried. We ate, talked, and took a lot of pictures. Then we brought out the cake and sang happy birthday. Some people near us even clapped for her. In the evening, we walked along the river together. My mom said it was her best birthday ever. That day is one of my favorite memories."}],
travel:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Tell me about a place in your country that you would recommend to foreign travelers. Why do you recommend it?", ko:"외국인 여행자에게 추천하고 싶은 당신 나라의 장소를 말해 주세요. 왜 추천하나요?",
  k:[["I’d recommend Jeju Island to foreign travelers.","외국인 여행자에게 제주도를 추천하고 싶어요."],
     ["It’s an island in the south of Korea.","한국 남쪽에 있는 섬이에요."],
     ["It has beautiful beaches and a famous mountain.","아름다운 해변과 유명한 산이 있어요."],
     ["You can try fresh seafood and black pork.","신선한 해산물과 흑돼지를 먹어 볼 수 있어요."],
     ["It’s the perfect place to relax.","쉬기에 완벽한 곳이에요."]],
  s:"I’d recommend Jeju Island to foreign travelers. It’s an island in the south of Korea, and it’s only an hour by plane from Seoul. It has beautiful beaches, green fields, and a famous mountain called Hallasan. You can also try fresh seafood and black pork, which are really delicious. The weather is warmer than in Seoul, too. It’s the perfect place to relax and enjoy nature.",
  m:"If a foreign friend visits Korea, I’d definitely recommend Jeju Island. It’s a big island in the south of Korea, and it’s only about an hour by plane from Seoul. Flights are cheap and frequent, so it’s easy to get there. There are three main reasons why I recommend it. First, the nature is amazing. It has beautiful beaches with clear blue water, green fields, and a famous mountain called Hallasan, which is the highest mountain in South Korea. There are also walking trails along the coast called Olle trails, and they have great views of the ocean. Second, the food is really delicious. You can try fresh seafood, like raw fish and abalone, and Jeju black pork, which is famous all over Korea. There are also lots of nice cafés with ocean views. Third, it’s very relaxing. Compared to Seoul, it’s quiet and slow, and the weather is warmer, too. You can rent a car and drive around the island at your own pace. I’ve been there four times, and I always have a great time. The only thing is that it gets really crowded in summer. So I’d recommend going in spring or fall. That’s why I recommend Jeju Island."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How has the way people travel changed compared to the past?", ko:"사람들이 여행하는 방식은 예전과 비교해 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["In the past, people often traveled in tour groups.","예전엔 사람들이 단체 관광을 많이 했어요."],
     ["They used paper maps and travel guidebooks.","종이 지도와 여행 책자를 썼어요."],
     ["Now people plan their trips with apps.","지금은 앱으로 여행을 계획해요."],
     ["Many people travel alone these days.","요즘은 혼자 여행하는 사람이 많아요."],
     ["It’s much easier to travel abroad now.","이제 해외여행이 훨씬 쉬워졌어요."]],
  s:"The way people travel has changed a lot. In the past, people often traveled in tour groups, and they used paper maps and guidebooks. Traveling abroad was expensive, so it was special. Now people plan their trips with apps. They book flights and hotels on their phones, and they use map apps to find places. Many people travel alone these days, too. It’s much easier and cheaper to travel abroad now.",
  m:"The way people travel has changed a lot compared to the past. When my parents were young, traveling abroad was really expensive and special. Most people traveled in tour groups, with a tour guide and a fixed schedule. They went to famous places, took pictures, and got back on the bus. They also used paper maps and big travel guidebooks, and they had to exchange money at the bank. If they got lost, they had to ask people for directions. These days, it’s totally different. People plan their trips with apps. They book cheap flights and hotels on their phones, read reviews, and use map apps to find places. They can even translate signs and menus with their phone cameras, so they don’t need to speak the language. Also, many people travel alone or with just one friend, and they make their own schedules. Some people even work remotely while they travel. Another big change is social media. Many people choose where to go based on pictures they see on Instagram. Personally, I think it’s much easier and cheaper to travel abroad now, and that’s great. But sometimes I think people spend too much time looking at their phones instead of enjoying the moment. That’s how travel has changed."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about your most memorable trip. Where did you go, who did you go with, and what made it special?", ko:"가장 기억에 남는 여행에 대해 말해 주세요. 어디에 누구와 갔고 무엇이 특별했나요?",
  k:[["My most memorable trip was to Da Nang in Vietnam.","가장 기억에 남는 여행은 베트남 다낭이었어요."],
     ["It was my first trip abroad with my parents.","부모님과 함께한 첫 해외여행이었어요."],
     ["We stayed at a resort near the beach.","해변 근처 리조트에 묵었어요."],
     ["My dad tried a lot of new food.","아빠가 새로운 음식을 많이 드셔 보셨어요."],
     ["I want to take them on another trip soon.","곧 다른 여행에 모시고 가고 싶어요."]],
  s:"My most memorable trip was to Da Nang in Vietnam two years ago. It was my first trip abroad with my parents. I paid for everything with my own money, so it was really special. We stayed at a resort near the beach for five days. We swam, ate a lot of delicious food, and visited a famous bridge. My parents were so happy. I want to take them on another trip soon.",
  m:"My most memorable trip was to Da Nang in Vietnam about two years ago. What made it special was that it was my first trip abroad with my parents. My parents had worked really hard their whole lives, and they had never been abroad together. So when I got my first bonus at work, I decided to take them on a trip, and I paid for everything with my own money. I planned everything myself, from the flights to the restaurants. It’s only about four and a half hours by plane from Korea, so it wasn’t too tiring for them. We stayed at a resort near the beach for five days. In the morning, we swam in the pool and walked on the beach. In the afternoon, we visited some famous places, like the Golden Bridge, which is held up by two giant stone hands. It was really amazing. The food was great, too. My dad tried a lot of new food, like pho and banh mi, and he loved it. My mom took hundreds of pictures. One night, we had dinner by the beach and watched the sunset together. My mom held my hand and thanked me. I almost cried. I want to take them on another trip soon."}],
jogging:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Why do you enjoy jogging or walking? How does it help you, both physically and mentally?", ko:"조깅이나 걷기를 왜 즐기나요? 몸과 마음에 어떻게 도움이 되나요?",
  k:[["I enjoy jogging because it’s simple and free.","조깅은 간단하고 돈이 안 들어서 좋아요."],
     ["You don’t need any special equipment.","특별한 장비가 필요 없어요."],
     ["Since I started jogging, I’ve lost five kilograms.","조깅을 시작한 뒤로 5킬로그램이 빠졌어요."],
     ["It also helps me clear my mind.","머리를 비우는 데도 도움이 돼요."],
     ["I sleep much better on the days I run.","뛴 날은 잠을 훨씬 잘 자요."]],
  s:"I enjoy jogging because it’s simple and free. You don’t need any special equipment, just a pair of good shoes. It helps me a lot physically. Since I started jogging, I’ve lost five kilograms, and I feel stronger. It also helps me mentally. When I run, I can clear my mind and forget about stress from work. I also sleep much better on the days I run. That’s why I love it.",
  m:"I really enjoy jogging, and there are a few reasons why. First of all, it’s simple and free. You don’t need to pay for a gym or buy any special equipment. You just need a pair of good running shoes and some comfortable clothes. You can do it anytime, anywhere, even when you’re traveling. Second, it helps me a lot physically. I sit at a desk all day at work, so I used to have back pain, and I gained a lot of weight. Since I started jogging about two years ago, I’ve lost five kilograms, and my back pain has gotten much better. I also have more energy during the day, and I don’t get tired as easily when I climb stairs. Third, and most importantly, it helps me mentally. My job is pretty stressful, and sometimes I feel really frustrated. But when I run, I can clear my mind and forget about my problems for a while. Sometimes I even come up with good ideas while I’m running. After jogging, I feel refreshed and positive. I also sleep much better on the days I run. For me, jogging isn’t just exercise. It’s my way of taking care of my body and my mind. That’s why I love it."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How have your exercise habits changed compared to when you were younger?", ko:"예전과 비교해 운동 습관이 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["When I was a student, I played soccer with my friends.","학생 때는 친구들과 축구를 했어요."],
     ["I never thought about my health back then.","그땐 건강에 대해 생각해 본 적이 없었어요."],
     ["After I started working, I stopped exercising.","일을 시작하고 운동을 그만뒀어요."],
     ["Now I try to jog three times a week.","지금은 일주일에 세 번 뛰려고 해요."],
     ["I exercise for my health, not just for fun.","재미뿐 아니라 건강을 위해 운동해요."]],
  s:"My exercise habits have changed a lot. When I was a student, I played soccer with my friends almost every day after school. I never thought about my health back then. It was just fun. After I started working, I was too busy, so I stopped exercising. I gained weight and got tired easily. So now I try to jog three times a week. These days, I exercise for my health, not just for fun.",
  m:"My exercise habits have changed a lot compared to when I was younger. When I was in middle school and high school, I was really active. I played soccer with my friends almost every day after school, and on weekends, we played basketball or rode bikes. I never thought about my health back then. Exercise was just fun, and it was a way to hang out with my friends. In college, I still played sports sometimes, but less often. Then, after I started working, everything changed. I was too busy and too tired, so I stopped exercising completely. I just went to work, came home, ate dinner, and watched TV. After a few years, I gained about ten kilograms, and I got tired easily. I even had some back pain. During a health checkup, the doctor told me I had to start exercising. That was a wake-up call. So I started jogging about two years ago. Now I try to jog three times a week, and I also do some stretching at home. These days, I exercise for my health, not just for fun. I also pay more attention to what I eat. I think that’s the biggest difference. As I got older, I realized how important health is."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about when you first started jogging or walking regularly. Why did you start, and how did it go at first?", ko:"처음 조깅이나 걷기를 꾸준히 시작했을 때를 말해 주세요. 왜 시작했고 처음엔 어땠나요?",
  k:[["I started jogging two years ago after a health checkup.","2년 전 건강검진 후 조깅을 시작했어요."],
     ["At first, I couldn’t run for more than five minutes.","처음엔 5분도 못 뛰었어요."],
     ["My legs hurt so much the next day.","다음 날 다리가 너무 아팠어요."],
     ["I almost gave up after the first week.","첫 주가 지나고 거의 포기할 뻔했어요."],
     ["Now I can run five kilometers without stopping.","지금은 쉬지 않고 5킬로미터를 뛸 수 있어요."]],
  s:"I started jogging about two years ago after a health checkup. The doctor said I needed to exercise. At first, it was really hard. I couldn’t run for more than five minutes, and my legs hurt so much the next day. I almost gave up after the first week. But I used a running app for beginners, and it helped a lot. Now I can run five kilometers without stopping. I’m really proud of myself.",
  m:"I remember clearly when I first started jogging. It was about two years ago, right after my health checkup. The doctor told me I had gained too much weight and that I needed to exercise regularly. I was a little shocked, so I decided to start jogging the next day. On the first day, I went to the river near my house, full of energy. But it was much harder than I expected. I couldn’t run for more than five minutes, and I was completely out of breath. I had to stop and walk for the rest of the way. The next day, my legs hurt so much that I could barely walk down the stairs. Honestly, I almost gave up after the first week. Then my friend told me about a running app for beginners. It tells you when to run and when to walk, and it slowly increases the time. So I followed the app three times a week. At first, I ran for one minute and walked for two minutes. Little by little, I got better. After two months, I could run for thirty minutes without stopping. Now I can run five kilometers easily, and I even joined a small race last year. I’m really proud of myself."}],
cafe:[
 {t:"묘사", en:"Tell me about cafés in your country. What are they like, and why do you think they are so popular?", ko:"당신 나라의 카페에 대해 말해 주세요. 어떤 모습이고 왜 그렇게 인기가 있다고 생각하나요?",
  k:[["There are cafés on almost every street in Korea.","한국엔 거의 모든 거리에 카페가 있어요."],
     ["Many people study or work at cafés.","많은 사람이 카페에서 공부하거나 일해요."],
     ["Some cafés have unique themes and interiors.","독특한 테마와 인테리어의 카페도 있어요."],
     ["Koreans drink a lot of iced Americano.","한국인은 아이스 아메리카노를 많이 마셔요."],
     ["Cafés are like a second living room.","카페는 제2의 거실 같아요."]],
  s:"There are cafés on almost every street in Korea. There are big chain cafés like Starbucks, and there are also many small, unique cafés. Many people study or work at cafés, so they’re often full of students with laptops. Some cafés have unique themes, like cafés with cats or plants. I think cafés are popular because Korean homes are small, so cafés are like a second living room.",
  m:"In Korea, there are cafés on almost every street. Sometimes you can find three or four cafés in one building. There are big chain cafés like Starbucks and Ediya, and there are also many small, independent cafés with unique styles. Some cafés have special themes, like cafés with cats or dogs, cafés full of plants, or cafés that look like they’re from Europe. Many young people visit these cafés just to take pictures for social media. Another interesting thing is that many people study or work at cafés. In the afternoon, you can see lots of students and office workers with laptops, and they stay for hours. Most cafés have free Wi-Fi and power outlets, so it’s very convenient. Also, Koreans drink a lot of iced Americano, even in the middle of winter. I think there are a few reasons why cafés are so popular in Korea. First, Korean homes are usually small, and many young people live with their parents. So cafés are like a second living room, where you can meet friends or have some time alone. Second, Korean people are really busy, and coffee gives them energy. Personally, I go to a café almost every day. That’s what cafés in Korea are like."},
 {t:"비교", en:"How have cafés changed compared to the past?", ko:"카페는 예전과 비교해 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["In the past, there were only a few coffee shops.","예전엔 커피숍이 몇 개 없었어요."],
     ["Most people drank instant coffee.","대부분 믹스커피를 마셨어요."],
     ["Now there are many kinds of coffee and desserts.","지금은 커피와 디저트 종류가 정말 많아요."],
     ["You can order with a kiosk or an app.","키오스크나 앱으로 주문할 수 있어요."],
     ["Coffee has become part of our daily lives.","커피가 일상의 일부가 됐어요."]],
  s:"Cafés have changed a lot. In the past, there were only a few coffee shops, and most people drank instant coffee at home or at work. Coffee shops were mostly for meetings or dates. Now there are cafés everywhere, and there are many kinds of coffee and desserts. You can also order with a kiosk or an app. Coffee has become part of our daily lives. I think it’s a big change.",
  m:"Cafés have changed a lot compared to the past. When my parents were young, there were only a few coffee shops, and they were called dabang. They were mostly places for business meetings or blind dates. The coffee wasn’t very special, and most people drank instant coffee mix at home or at work. Even when I was in middle school, there weren’t many cafés in my neighborhood. Then, in the early two thousands, big chain cafés like Starbucks came to Korea, and things started to change. Now there are cafés everywhere, and there are so many kinds of coffee, like lattes, cold brew, and hand-drip coffee. There are also lots of desserts, like cakes, macarons, and croffles. Another big change is how we order. These days, you can order with a kiosk, or you can order on an app before you arrive and just pick it up. Also, cafés have become places where people study and work for hours, not just places to drink coffee. Prices have gone up a lot, too. An Americano is about five thousand won now. Overall, coffee has become part of our daily lives. Many people, including me, can’t start the day without a cup of coffee. That’s how cafés have changed."},
 {t:"경험", en:"Tell me about a memorable conversation or meeting you had at a café.", ko:"카페에서 있었던 기억에 남는 대화나 만남에 대해 말해 주세요.",
  k:[["I met my best friend from high school at a café.","고등학교 단짝 친구를 카페에서 만났어요."],
     ["We hadn’t seen each other for five years.","5년 동안 서로 못 봤어요."],
     ["At first, it felt a little awkward.","처음엔 조금 어색했어요."],
     ["But soon we were laughing like the old days.","하지만 곧 옛날처럼 웃고 있었어요."],
     ["We talked for four hours without noticing.","시간 가는 줄 모르고 4시간이나 얘기했어요."]],
  s:"Last year, I met my best friend from high school at a café. We hadn’t seen each other for five years, because she moved abroad. At first, it felt a little awkward. But soon we were laughing like the old days. We talked about our school days, our jobs, and our families. We talked for four hours without noticing. When we left, we promised to meet more often. It was a really special day.",
  m:"I still remember a really special meeting I had at a café last year. I met my best friend from high school, Jiyoung. We were really close in high school, but after graduation, she moved to Canada for college. At first, we talked on the phone a lot, but we both got busy, and we slowly lost touch. We hadn’t seen each other for about five years. Then one day, she sent me a message saying she was visiting Korea for two weeks. I was so excited. We decided to meet at a café near our old high school. When I walked in, I recognized her right away, but at first, it felt a little awkward. We didn’t know what to say. But after a few minutes, we started talking about our school days, like our crazy teachers and the trips we took together. Soon we were laughing like the old days. We also talked about our jobs, our families, and our worries. She said living abroad was lonely sometimes. We talked for four hours without noticing, and the café was about to close. When we left, we hugged and promised to keep in touch. Now we video chat every month. It was one of the best days of last year."}],
roleplay:[
 {t:"롤플레이", en:"Please act out this situation. You want to join a gym near your home. Call the gym and ask three or four questions to find out about membership.", ko:"상황극입니다. 집 근처 헬스장에 등록하려고 해요. 헬스장에 전화해 회원권에 대해 3~4가지 질문하세요.",
  k:[["Hi, I’m thinking about joining your gym.","안녕하세요, 헬스장 등록을 생각 중이에요."],
     ["How much is a monthly membership?","한 달 회원권은 얼마인가요?"],
     ["What are your opening hours?","운영 시간이 어떻게 되나요?"],
     ["Do you offer personal training?","개인 트레이닝도 하나요?"],
     ["Can I come in and look around first?","먼저 가서 둘러봐도 될까요?"]],
  s:"Hi, I’m thinking about joining your gym, and I have a few questions. First, how much is a monthly membership? And is it cheaper if I sign up for three months? Also, what are your opening hours? I usually work out after nine at night. Do you offer personal training, too? Lastly, can I come in and look around first? Great. Thank you so much.",
  m:"Hi, I’m calling because I’m thinking about joining your gym. I just moved to this neighborhood, and your gym is really close to my apartment. I have a few questions, if that’s okay. First, how much is a monthly membership? I see. And is it cheaper if I sign up for three months or six months? Oh, that’s a good deal. Does that include a locker and workout clothes? Great. Next, what are your opening hours? I usually work late, so I’d like to work out after nine at night. You’re open until midnight? Perfect. How about on weekends? Okay, that works for me. Also, do you offer personal training? I haven’t exercised in a long time, so I think I need some help at first. How much is it per session? I see. Do you have any group classes, like yoga or spinning? That sounds fun. One more thing, is there a parking lot? Sometimes I might drive there. Okay. Lastly, can I come in and look around first before I sign up? Maybe tomorrow evening? Great. And can I try it for one day for free? Wonderful. Thank you so much for your help. I’ll see you tomorrow. Bye."},
 {t:"롤플레이", en:"Please act out this situation. You bought a new phone, but it stopped working after two days. Go to the store, explain the problem, and suggest two or three solutions.", ko:"상황극입니다. 새 휴대폰을 샀는데 이틀 만에 작동이 멈췄어요. 가게에 가서 문제를 설명하고 해결책을 2~3가지 제안하세요.",
  k:[["Excuse me, I bought this phone here two days ago.","실례합니다, 이틀 전에 여기서 이 휴대폰을 샀어요."],
     ["It suddenly stopped turning on.","갑자기 전원이 안 켜져요."],
     ["I didn’t drop it or get it wet.","떨어뜨리거나 물에 젖게 한 적 없어요."],
     ["Could I exchange it for a new one?","새 걸로 교환할 수 있을까요?"],
     ["If not, I’d like a full refund.","안 되면 전액 환불받고 싶어요."]],
  s:"Excuse me, I bought this phone here two days ago, but it suddenly stopped turning on. I charged it all night, but nothing happened. I didn’t drop it or get it wet. Here’s my receipt. Could I exchange it for a new one? If you don’t have one in stock, could you lend me a phone while it’s being fixed? If not, I’d like a full refund. Thank you.",
  m:"Excuse me, I have a problem with a phone I bought here. I bought this phone two days ago, right here at this store. Here’s my receipt. On the first day, it worked fine. But yesterday evening, the screen suddenly went black, and now it won’t turn on at all. I charged it all night with the charger that came in the box, and I tried pressing the power button for a long time, but nothing happened. I didn’t drop it or get it wet. It’s brand new, and I’ve been really careful with it. This is a big problem for me, because I use my phone for work, and I have to contact my clients today. So I’d like to suggest a few solutions. First, could I exchange it for a new one right now? I think that would be the best option, since I bought it only two days ago. If you don’t have the same model in stock, could you lend me a phone to use while it’s being repaired? And please tell me how long the repair will take. If neither of those is possible, I’d like a full refund, and I’ll buy a different phone. I hope you understand my situation. Please let me know what you can do. Thank you."},
 {t:"롤플레이", en:"Have you ever had a problem with a reservation or something you bought? Tell me what happened and how you dealt with it.", ko:"예약이나 산 물건 때문에 문제를 겪은 적이 있나요? 무슨 일이 있었고 어떻게 대처했는지 말해 주세요.",
  k:[["Last year, I booked a hotel online for a trip.","작년에 여행 가려고 온라인으로 호텔을 예약했어요."],
     ["When I arrived, they said there was no reservation.","도착하니 예약이 없다고 했어요."],
     ["I showed them the confirmation email.","확인 메일을 보여줬어요."],
     ["They finally found me a room.","결국 방을 하나 구해 줬어요."],
     ["Now I always call the hotel before I go.","이제는 가기 전에 항상 호텔에 전화해요."]],
  s:"Last year, I booked a hotel online for a trip to Busan. When I arrived, the front desk said there was no reservation under my name. I was really shocked. I showed them the confirmation email on my phone. They checked again and said there was a problem with the website. They finally found me a room, and they gave me free breakfast. Now I always call the hotel before I go.",
  m:"Yes, I had a problem with a reservation last year. I was planning a weekend trip to Busan with my friend, so I booked a hotel online about a month early. I paid in advance, and I got a confirmation email. On the day of the trip, we took the train to Busan and arrived at the hotel around nine at night. We were really tired. But when I gave my name at the front desk, the staff said there was no reservation under my name. I was really shocked, and I didn’t know what to do. It was a holiday weekend, so I knew all the other hotels would be full. I stayed calm and showed them the confirmation email on my phone. The staff checked their system again and called the manager. The manager said there was a problem with the booking website, and our reservation didn’t go through to the hotel. He apologized many times. Luckily, they had one room left, and it was even bigger than the one I booked. They also gave us free breakfast for two days. In the end, it turned out fine. But I learned a lesson. Now I always call the hotel a few days before I go to check my reservation. That’s what happened."}],
surprise:[
 {t:"돌발", en:"Tell me about the weather and seasons in your country. Which season do you like best, and why?", ko:"당신 나라의 날씨와 계절에 대해 말해 주세요. 어떤 계절을 가장 좋아하고 왜인가요?",
  k:[["Korea has four distinct seasons.","한국은 사계절이 뚜렷해요."],
     ["Summer is hot and humid, with a rainy season.","여름은 덥고 습하고 장마가 있어요."],
     ["Winter is very cold and dry.","겨울은 아주 춥고 건조해요."],
     ["My favorite season is fall.","제가 가장 좋아하는 계절은 가을이에요."],
     ["These days, spring and fall are getting shorter.","요즘은 봄과 가을이 점점 짧아지고 있어요."]],
  s:"Korea has four distinct seasons. Spring is warm, and there are lots of flowers. Summer is hot and humid, and there’s a rainy season in July. Fall is cool and clear, and the leaves turn red and yellow. Winter is very cold and dry, and sometimes it snows. My favorite season is fall, because the weather is perfect for walking. But these days, spring and fall are getting shorter.",
  m:"Korea has four distinct seasons, and each season is really different. Spring is from March to May. It’s warm, and there are lots of flowers, like cherry blossoms. Many people go on picnics. But there’s a lot of fine dust in spring, so people often wear masks. Summer is from June to August. It’s really hot and humid, and the temperature often goes over thirty-five degrees. There’s also a rainy season in July, when it rains almost every day. Fall is from September to November. It’s cool and clear, the sky is really blue, and the leaves turn red and yellow. Winter is from December to February. It’s very cold and dry, and it sometimes goes down to minus fifteen degrees. Sometimes it snows, too. My favorite season is definitely fall. The weather is perfect, not too hot and not too cold, so it’s great for walking, jogging, and hiking. I also love the colorful leaves in the mountains. On the other hand, I don’t like summer, because I sweat a lot and can’t sleep well at night. These days, because of climate change, summers are getting longer and hotter, and spring and fall are getting shorter. That makes me a little sad."},
 {t:"돌발", en:"Tell me about banks in your country. What do people usually do at the bank, and how has banking changed?", ko:"당신 나라의 은행에 대해 말해 주세요. 사람들은 은행에서 주로 무엇을 하고, 은행 업무는 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["Most banks in Korea open at nine and close at four.","한국 은행 대부분은 9시에 열고 4시에 닫아요."],
     ["People go to the bank to open an account or get a loan.","계좌를 만들거나 대출받으러 은행에 가요."],
     ["You have to take a number and wait.","번호표를 뽑고 기다려야 해요."],
     ["These days, most people use banking apps.","요즘은 대부분 은행 앱을 써요."],
     ["I haven’t been to a bank in almost a year.","거의 1년 동안 은행에 안 갔어요."]],
  s:"Most banks in Korea open at nine and close at four on weekdays. People go to the bank to open an account, get a loan, or exchange money. When you go in, you take a number and wait. In the past, people went to the bank often. But these days, most people use banking apps on their phones. You can send money in seconds. I haven’t been to a bank in almost a year.",
  m:"In Korea, there are many banks, and you can find a few branches in every neighborhood. Most banks open at nine in the morning and close at four in the afternoon on weekdays, so it’s hard for office workers to visit them. People usually go to the bank to open an account, get a credit card, get a loan, or exchange money before a trip. When you go into a bank, you take a number from a machine and wait until your number is called. Then you sit at a counter and talk to a bank teller. It can take a long time, especially at lunchtime. Banking has changed a lot compared to the past. When I was a kid, my mom went to the bank almost every week to pay bills and send money. She had to fill out paper forms and stamp them. Now most people use banking apps on their phones. You can send money to anyone in a few seconds, check your account, and even get a loan without going to the bank. There are also internet-only banks with no branches at all. Personally, I haven’t been to a bank in almost a year. It’s really convenient. But older people sometimes find the apps difficult, so they still go to the bank."},
 {t:"돌발", en:"What do people in your country do to stay healthy? What do you personally do to stay healthy?", ko:"당신 나라 사람들은 건강을 위해 무엇을 하나요? 당신은 개인적으로 무엇을 하나요?",
  k:[["Koreans care a lot about their health.","한국인은 건강에 관심이 많아요."],
     ["Many people go hiking on weekends.","많은 사람이 주말에 등산을 가요."],
     ["Some people take vitamins every day.","매일 비타민을 먹는 사람도 있어요."],
     ["I try to eat more vegetables and drink less.","채소를 더 먹고 술을 덜 마시려고 해요."],
     ["Getting enough sleep is the most important thing.","충분히 자는 게 가장 중요해요."]],
  s:"Koreans care a lot about their health. Many people go hiking on weekends, and a lot of people go to the gym after work. Some people take vitamins or health supplements every day. Also, Korean food has a lot of vegetables, so it’s pretty healthy. Personally, I jog three times a week, and I try to eat more vegetables and drink less. I think getting enough sleep is the most important thing, too.",
  m:"I think Koreans care a lot about their health. You can see that in many ways. First, a lot of people exercise. On weekends, many people go hiking in the mountains, especially middle-aged people. You can see them on the subway wearing colorful hiking clothes. Young people usually go to the gym, do pilates, or play sports like tennis and golf. Running has also become really popular recently. Second, many people take vitamins or health supplements every day, like vitamin C, omega-three, or red ginseng. Red ginseng is a famous Korean health product, and people often give it as a gift. Third, Korean food is generally healthy, because it has a lot of vegetables and fermented food, like kimchi. Also, every company in Korea gives its workers a free health checkup every year or two. Personally, I try to stay healthy in a few ways. I jog three times a week along the river, and I take the stairs instead of the elevator at work. I also try to eat more vegetables and drink less, although it’s hard because I have a lot of company dinners. And I think getting enough sleep is the most important thing. I try to go to bed before midnight. That’s how people stay healthy in Korea."},
 {t:"돌발", en:"Talk about online shopping in your country. What do people buy online, and how has it changed the way people shop?", ko:"당신 나라의 온라인 쇼핑에 대해 이야기해 주세요. 사람들은 온라인으로 무엇을 사고, 쇼핑 방식은 어떻게 바뀌었나요?",
  k:[["Online shopping is really popular in Korea.","한국에선 온라인 쇼핑이 정말 인기예요."],
     ["You can buy almost anything with a few taps.","몇 번만 누르면 거의 뭐든 살 수 있어요."],
     ["If you order at night, it arrives the next morning.","밤에 주문하면 다음 날 아침에 와요."],
     ["I buy groceries and clothes online.","저는 장보기와 옷을 온라인으로 사요."],
     ["Sometimes I buy things I don’t really need.","가끔 꼭 필요하지 않은 걸 사기도 해요."]],
  s:"Online shopping is really popular in Korea. You can buy almost anything with a few taps on your phone, like clothes, food, and furniture. Delivery is very fast. If you order at night, it arrives the next morning. I buy groceries and clothes online, because it saves time. But it’s so easy that sometimes I buy things I don’t really need. Also, there’s a lot of packaging waste.",
  m:"Online shopping is really popular in Korea, maybe more than in any other country. You can buy almost anything with a few taps on your phone, like clothes, groceries, electronics, furniture, and even fresh fish. The most amazing thing is the delivery. If you order before midnight, it usually arrives at your door the next morning, sometimes even before seven a.m. That’s called dawn delivery. Delivery is often free if you have a membership. Because of this, the way people shop has changed a lot. In the past, people went to big supermarkets on weekends to buy groceries for the whole week. They also went to department stores to buy clothes. Now many people just order everything online, and some supermarkets and stores have closed. Also, people compare prices and read reviews before they buy anything, so it’s easier to find good deals. Personally, I buy groceries and clothes online, because I’m busy and it saves a lot of time. I usually order on my phone on the subway. On the other hand, there are some problems. It’s so easy that sometimes I buy things I don’t really need. Also, there’s a lot of packaging waste, like boxes and plastic. So I try to order less often and buy things all at once."}]
};

// 합치기: 짧은 답안 s, 2분 답안 m, 새 문항 추가
TOPICS.forEach(t=>{
  t.qs.forEach((q,qi)=>{ const L=LONG[t.id+":"+qi]; if(L){ q.s=q.m; q.m=L; } });
  (MORE[t.id]||[]).forEach(q=>t.qs.push(q));
});

// 만능 표현: 답변을 길게 늘리는 연결 문장
UNIV.push({g:"길게 늘리기", items:[
  ["Let me give you a specific example.","구체적인 예를 하나 들어 볼게요."],
  ["There are two main reasons why I like it.","제가 그걸 좋아하는 이유는 크게 두 가지예요."],
  ["Compared to the past, it has changed a lot.","예전과 비교하면 많이 바뀌었어요."],
  ["On the other hand, there are some downsides, too.","반면에 단점도 몇 가지 있어요."],
  ["Honestly, I didn’t expect that at all.","솔직히 전혀 예상 못 했어요."],
  ["I learned an important lesson from that experience.","그 경험에서 중요한 교훈을 얻었어요."]]});
